    {
      "heading": "Question 2: methane fuel cell",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "At the anode, methane and water give CO two, 8 H plus and 8 electrons.",
          "write": "CH₄ + 2H₂O → CO₂ + 8H⁺ + 8e⁻"
        },
        {
          "say": "Five amps for 7200 seconds is 36 000 coulombs, or 0.3731 moles of electrons.",
          "write": "n(e⁻) = 0.3731 mol"
        },
        {
          "say": "Eight electrons per methane, so divide by 8.",
          "write": "n(CH₄) = 0.04663 mol",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Eight electrons per methane",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "8 mol e⁻"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 250,
                "y": 130,
                "x2": 330,
                "y2": 130,
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 340,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "1 mol CH₄",
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Times 24.8 gives 1.16 litres of methane.",
          "write": "V = 1.16 L"
        },
        {
          "say": "21.6 kilojoules out of 41.5 available. Efficiency is 52 percent.",
          "write": "52%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Question 3: equilibrium",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "An ICE table gives 0.100, 0.150 and 0.300 moles at equilibrium.",
          "write": "2 : 1 : 2 ratio"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide by two litres, then substitute. K is 120.",
          "write": "K = 120 M⁻¹"
        },
        {
          "say": "A new mixture has Q equal to 40. Less than K, so shift right.",
          "write": "Q 40 < K 120 → right",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
